+// Decode matmul: one tile row of BF16 activations times DRAM-interleaved
+// weights, as in LLM decode, where streaming the weights from DRAM is the
+// whole cost. The output tiles are split as evenly as possible over the
+// worker grid, the activation row is multicast once per grid row and stays
+// resident in L1, and each core streams its weight blocks of in0_block_w K
+// tiles on both NOCs. Every output tile accumulates over all of K in FP32
+// DST. A bias is a single tile row added to every row, as in the 1D matmul.
+//
